	(text "VALUE CHOICES - CN3801 (1S LiFePO4 buck charger)\n- CV = 3.625 V, fixed inside the CN3801 (LFP version): no feedback divider.\n- Charge current  I_CC = 120 mV / R16 = 120 mV / 47 mR = 2.55 A.   R16 dissipation 2.55^2 x 0.047 = 0.31 W (0.5 W part).\n- MPPT / input-sag limit:  VCC >= 1.205 V x (1 + R3/R4) = 1.205 x (1 + 274k/100k) = 4.51 V\n    -> the charger reduces current instead of pulling a weak USB source below 4.5 V.\n- R5 120 R + C4 220 nF on COM: loop compensation, datasheet values.\n- C3 100 nF is VG-to-VCC (not to GND): gate-driver supply, per datasheet.\n- U302 LM74700 + Q303 (ideal diode, was SS54 D1) blocks the pack back-feeding VBUS through the Q1 body diode. D303 SMAJ12A = VBUS TVS.  D2 SS54 = freewheel diode.\n- L1 10 uH, Isat 5.5 A  >  2.55 A charge current + ripple.\n- CHG_OFF: R6 100k keeps Q2 off -> charging enabled by default.  ESP_CHG_OFF high -> Q2 pulls MPPT low -> charge stops\n    (bench-verify).  R7 1k limits the GPIO current.\n- CHRG / DONE are open-drain: R8 / R9 10k pull-ups to +3V3.\n- NTC: NTC_ADC = 3.3 V x R_NTC / (R31 + R_NTC) = 1.65 V at 25 C (R31 = R_NTC(25C) = 10k).\n    Firmware stops charging outside 0..45 C via CHG_OFF.  Place TH1 against the main cell.\n- Layout: route CHG_CSP and the BAT (P+) sense line as a Kelvin pair from the R16 pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 85.09 124.968 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2641ec4c-31a8-4b0b-b5de-2650b83211a2")
	)
	(text "Q303 ~0.2 W at 2.2 A input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.56 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
